    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526693": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Social Work (Welsh Language Essential)",
      "description": "2526693 Lecturer in Social Work (Welsh Language Essential) - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526693 Lecturer in Social Work (Welsh Language Essential) Lecturer in Social Work (Welsh Language Essential) We are seeking to appoint a 0.4 FTE Lecturer in Social Work to teach across the suite of undergraduate and postgraduate Social Work programmes. This is an exciting opportunity to shape the future Social Work workforce, and to join a creative, dynamic, and values driven team, which places co-production and participation at the heart of all we do. About the role: You will teach across undergraduate and postgraduate Social Work programmes, creating and delivering high-quality learning, teaching and student support.  You will support students on their placements, liaising with placement providers, and maintaining strong links with the sector. You will support students who choose to study through the medium of Welsh. About you: We are looking for someone who is: a registered and qualified Social Worker educated to masters level or beyond a confident and effective communicator competent and confident in using the Welsh Language motivated to deliver high-quality teaching and learning at undergraduate and postgraduate level skilled in facilitating engaging, interactive learning opportunities solution focused, with a strong team work ethic This fractional role is ideal for someone who wishes to combine ongoing professional practice with teaching in Higher Education allowing them to develop their skills in teaching and learning. If you are interested in learning more about this role, please contact Rachel Byron rachel.byron@wrexham.ac.uk Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is a signatory to the Researcher Development Concordat and Research Integrity Concordat. The University is committed to the principles of these concordats and is dedicated to the development of researchers in all posts and upholding the highest standards of rigour and integrity in all aspects of research. Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Social Work and Therapeutic Childcare Location Wrexham Salary £16,426 to £17,898\n              per annum Post Type Part Time Hours per Week 14.8 Closing Date Sunday 13 September 2026 Reference 2526693 DBS A DBS may be required for this position Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are essential Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526749": {
      "title": "Sports Partnership Impact Manager",
      "description": "2526749 Sports Partnership Impact Manager - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526749 Sports Partnership Impact Manager Sports Partnership Impact Manager Fixed term for 24 months We are seeking an ambitious and collaborative Sports Partnership Impact Manager to help shape the future of sport, health, and community wellbeing across Wrexham. This exciting role will be central to the development of the Wrexham Sports Partnership, working with key partners including Wrexham University, Wrexham AFC Foundation, and Wrexham County Borough Council. You will lead on research, evaluation, and insight— using data to evidence and communicate the life-changing impact of sport across our communities. You will design and deliver innovative research and evaluation approaches, develop data frameworks, and produce high-quality reports and insights. You’ll also play a key role in partnership working—bringing organisations together to inform strategy, shape investment, and support inclusive community programmes. You’ll bring: Strong analytical and research skills (quantitative and qualitative) Experience of evaluation, reporting, and project delivery Excellent communication and partnership-building abilities A passion for sport’s role in improving health, inclusion, and community wellbeing A relevant degree is essential, with postgraduate or equivalent research experience desirable. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to Wrexham’s ambition as a modern civic university, helping to deliver meaningful social impact through sport and collaboration across the region. Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Secretariat Location Wrexham Salary £32,851 to £35,796\n              per annum Post Type Part Time Fixed Term 24 months Hours per Week 29.6 Closing Date Monday 07 September 2026 Reference 2526749 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Roa