    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526791": {
      "title": "Planning Manager",
      "description": "2526791 Planning Manager - Business Intelligence - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526791 Planning Manager - Business Intelligence Planning Manager - Business Intelligence This is a maternity cover post for the duration of up to 12 months. This is an exciting opportunity to join Wrexham University’s Planning and Reporting team as it continues to develop and enhance the institution’s Business Intelligence capabilities. With the recent implementation of a data warehouse, this role will lead on developing and embedding BI reporting processes, particularly in light of the current data warehouse project coming to fruition, which will enable new approaches to data analysis and reporting. The post-holder will lead and direct a sub-team within Planning and Reporting that will be responsible for the development and implementation of a new range of Business Intelligence dashboards that will provide access to key data and information across the institution. This role will be an integral part of embedding the use of Business Intelligence as a core part of both the University’s strategic decision making as well as day-to-day data provision. This will include overseeing the development of PowerBI dashboards supporting a wide range of areas, such as student number modelling, analysis of application and enrolment trends and institutional KPIs. They will be required to coordinate and plan significant University-wide processes, developing effective relationships across the University, and will be expected to analyse, interpret and clearly communicate complex information to influence strategic planning and policy development. If you would like an informal discussion regarding this opportunity, please email simon.beer@wrexham.ac.uk Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Planning and Reporting Location Wrexham Salary £41,064 to £44,745\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Fixed Term 12 months Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Reference 2526791 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Ope