      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Dietetics",
      "description": "2526835 Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Dietetics - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526835 Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Dietetics Senior Lecturer in Nutrition and Dietetics Senior Lecturer Nutrition and Dietetics We are seeking an enthusiastic and motivated HCPC-registered Dietitian to join our Allied Health Professions team as a Senior Lecturer. The successful applicant will contribute to teaching, assessment, student support and curriculum development across the AHP portfolio, whilst providing specialist expertise within Nutrition and Dietetics. Candidates should have relevant professional experience, experience of higher education teaching and assessment, and the ability to contribute to interprofessional learning and collaborative working across programmes. Applicants should demonstrate a commitment to delivering an excellent student experience and contributing to the wider activities and development of the School and University. Welsh language skills are desirable. Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is a signatory to the Researcher Development Concordat and Research Integrity Concordat. The University is committed to the principles of 