    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526841": {
      "title": "Director of Campus and Place",
      "description": "2526841 Director of Campus and Place - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526841 Director of Campus and Place Director of Campus and Place Shape the future of our campuses.  Drive regeneration.  Deliver lasting impact. Wrexham University is seeking an exceptional and visionary leader to join our senior leadership team as Director of Campus and Place. Reporting directly to the Chief Finance and Operating Officer, this is a unique opportunity to lead the continuing transformation of our estate, infrastructure and place-making agenda as we deliver our ambitious Wrexham 2030 Vision and Strategy. As a modern civic university, we are committed to creating outstanding environments that inspire learning, innovation, enterprise and community engagement. We are looking for a strategic leader who can unlock the full potential of our physical estate, ensuring it supports exceptional student experiences, drives commercial opportunities and contributes to the economic, social and cultural development of North Wales. About the Role The Director of Campus and Place will provide strategic leadership across estates, capital projects, facilities management, campus services and commercial property development. You will lead the development and delivery of a University-wide Campus and Place Strategy, creating a coherent vision that integrates physical infrastructure, digital connectivity, sustainability, security and commercialisation, across multiple campuses. Key responsibilities include: Leading the University's long-term campus master planning and estate strategy. Delivering major capital investment and regeneration programmes. Championing sustainability and driving progress towards net zero ambitions. Creating innovative, flexible and inclusive learning and social environments. Maximising the value of University assets through commercialisation and strategic partnerships. Supporting the growth of enterprise, innovation and research spaces. Building strong relationships with government, funding bodies, industry, investors, local authorities and community stakeholders. Ensuring operational excellence, compliance, health and safety, and effective campus services. About You We are seeking an influential and collaborative leader with a strong track record of delivering transformational change in complex organisations. You will bring: Essential Experience and Expertise Significant senior leadership experience in estates, infrastructure, regeneration, property and/or major capital development environments. Proven success delivering complex capital programmes and organisational transformation. Experience developing and implementing long-term estate strategies, across multiple sites. Demonstrable success in generating commercial income from property or infrastructure assets. Expertise in managing substantial budgets, resources and risks. Strong stakeholder engagement and partnership-building skills. Experience securing external investment and funding. Knowledge of health and safety, compliance and building maintenance legislation. An inclusive and people-focused approach to leading large, diverse teams Experience advising executive teams and governing bodies on strategic estate and infrastructure investment decisions. If you would like an informal discussion regarding this opportunity, please email joy.morton@wrexham.ac.uk Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Estates Central Location Wrexham Salary £83,073 to £113,890\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Closing Date Wednesday 16 September 2026 Interview Date Thursday 01 October 2026 Reference 2526841 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526856": {
      "title": "Head of Health, Safety and Compliance",
      "description": "2526856 Head of Health, Safety and Compliance - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526856 Head of Health, Safety and Compliance Head of Health, Safety and Compliance We are looking for a credible and influential Head of Health, Safety and Compliance to join our multi-site University and who drive cultural and behavioural change. The individual should have significant leadership experience gained within a complex environment with demonstrable strong knowledge of UK health, safety and environmental legislation. This is a highly visible position, requiring an individual who can build credibility at every level from engaging frontline teams to influencing senior stakeholders and presenting and reporting at committees and at Board level. The individual should be experienced in championing a proactive safety culture and continuous improvement mindset across multiple sites ensuring compliance with all health and safety and environmental legislation, permits and regulatory requirements. Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Safety, Health and Environment Location Wrexham Salary £51,754 to £56,535\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Closing Date Sunday 13 September 2026 Reference 2526856 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526SESSPOOLART": {
      "title": "Sessional Lecturer",
      "description": "2526SESSPOOLART Sessional Lecturer - Art & Design - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526SESSPOOLART Sessional Lecturer - Art & Design Sessional Lecturer - Art & Design Location: Wrexham University, Wrexham, with teaching assignments in China Contract: Sessional Lecturer Pool – Flexible Teaching Assignments Teaching Periods: Flexible teaching opportunities during Semester 1 and Semester 2, including periods of international delivery in China. Salary: Competitive hourly teaching rate. Where international teaching is required, flights, accommodation, subsistence and appropriate local support will be provided in accordance with University arrangements. Wrexham University is seeking experienced academics and creative industry professionals to join our Art & Design Sessional Lecturer Pool, with an initial focus on supporting the delivery of our growing Transnational Education (TNE) provision. Alongside our TNE provision, sessional lecturers will become part of the wider Art & Design academic community at Wrexham University, working collaboratively with our existing academic teams and contributing specialist knowledge, professional practice and teaching expertise across our Art and Design portfolio where opportunities and programme requirements arise. Successful applicants will support our established partnerships in Chongqing and Tonghua, China, contributing to the delivery of Wrexham University Art and Design programmes. This will include periods of teaching at our partner institutions in China, with assignments planned according to programme requirements and individual areas of academic, creative and professional expertise. These roles provide an opportunity to contribute to Wrexham University’s international ambitions while maintaining a strong connection with teaching and academic activity at Wrexham. Sessional lecturers will work with colleagues across both Wrexham University and our international partners, supporting a consistent, high-quality student experience across our home and TNE provision. Subject Areas We are particularly interested in applicants with knowledge and experience across areas such as: Graphic and Communication Design Digital and Motion Design Illustration UI Design Advertising Creative Practice Visual Communication Design Research Critical and Creative Thinking Social Design Exhibition and Display Design Print and Publication Design Teaching requirements will vary according to programme needs and may include studio teaching, lectures, seminars, workshops, tutorials, assessment, critique and other associated academic activities. International teaching may be delivered through intensive teaching blocks, typically between 2 and 8 weeks, depending on programme and institutional requirements. What We're Looking For Applicants should have: A postgraduate qualification in Art, Design or a closely related discipline. Higher education teaching experience or significant relevant creative industry experience. The ability to deliver engaging, inclusive and practice-based teaching. Strong communication and organisational skills. The ability to work collaboratively alongside established academic teams. A flexible approach to teaching across different academic and cultural environments. The flexibility to contribute to teaching at Wrexham University and undertake international teaching assignments where required. Experience of Transnational Education or international teaching and Fellowship of Advance HE or an equivalent teaching qualification would be advantageous. What We Offer Successful applicants will join our Art & Design Sessional Lecturer Pool and may be offered teaching assignments according to programme requirements, availability and their areas of expertise. The opportunity provides: Competitive hourly teaching rates. Opportunities to work alongside existing academic teams at Wrexham University. Opportunities to contribute specialist academic and professional expertise to our Art and Design provision. Experience across different programmes and teaching environments. Opportunities to contribute to Wrexham University’s international and TNE partnerships. Opportunities to develop international teaching experience and professional networks. Where international teaching is required, return international travel, accommodation, subsistence and appropriate local support in accordance with University arrangements. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Wrexham University is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion and welcomes applications from suitably qualified candidates from all backgrounds. We will make reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process where required. How to Apply To join our Art & Design Sessional Lecturer Pool, please complete the application form and upload any supporting documents to outline your teaching and/or industry experience and engineering specialisms. Closing Date 7 th of September 2026 Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Engineering Location Wrexham Salary per hour Post Type Casual Closing Date Monday 07 September 2026 Reference 2526SESSPOOLART Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2526SESSPOOLENG": {
      "title": "Sessional Lecturer",
      "description": "2526SESSPOOLENG Sessional Lecturer - Engineering - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2526SESSPOOLENG Sessional Lecturer - Engineering Sessional Lecturer - Engineering Location: Wrexham University, Wrexham, with teaching assignments in China Contract: Sessional Lecturer Pool – Flexible Teaching Assignments Teaching Periods: Flexible teaching opportunities during Semester 1 and Semester 2, including periods of international delivery in China. Salary: Competitive hourly teaching rate. Where international teaching is required, flights, accommodation, subsistence and appropriate local support will be provided in accordance with University arrangements. Wrexham University is seeking experienced academics and industry professionals to join our Engineering Sessional Lecturer Pool, with an initial focus on supporting the delivery of our growing Transnational Education (TNE) provision. Alongside our TNE provision, sessional lecturers will become part of the wider Engineering academic community at Wrexham University, working collaboratively with our existing academic teams and contributing to teaching and learning across our Engineering portfolio where opportunities and programme requirements arise. Successful applicants will support our established partnership with Dalian Polytechnic University in China, contributing to the delivery of the BEng (Hons) Mechatronics Engineering programme. This will include periods of teaching at our partner institution in China, with assignments planned according to programme requirements and individual areas of expertise. These roles provide an opportunity to contribute to Wrexham University’s international ambitions while maintaining a strong connection with teaching and academic activity at Wrexham. Sessional lecturers will work with colleagues across both Wrexham University and our international partners, supporting a consistent, high-quality student experience across our home and TNE provision. Subject Areas We are particularly interested in applicants with expertise in one or more of the following: Electrical Engineering Instrumentation and Control Industrial Electronics and Applications Mechatronics Applications Electronics Technology Industrial Automation and PLCs Teaching requirements will vary according to programme needs and may include lectures, seminars, practical and laboratory sessions, tutorials, assessment and other associated academic activities. International teaching may be delivered through intensive teaching blocks, typically approximately 6–8 weeks, depending on programme and institutional requirements. What We're Looking For Applicants should have: A postgraduate qualification in Engineering or a closely related discipline. Higher education teaching experience or significant relevant industrial experience. The ability to deliver engaging, inclusive and student-centred teaching. The ability to contribute effectively to practical and laboratory-based learning where appropriate. Strong communication and organisational skills. A collaborative approach and the ability to work effectively alongside established academic teams. The flexibility to contribute to teaching at Wrexham University and undertake international teaching assignments where required. The following are desirable: Fellowship of Advance HE or an HE teaching qualification. Chartered Engineer (CEng), Incorporated Engineer (IEng) or professional body membership. Experience of Transnational Education or international teaching. What We Offer Successful applicants will join our Engineering Sessional Lecturer Pool and may be offered teaching assignments according to programme requirements, availability and their areas of expertise. Competitive hourly teaching rates. Opportunities to work alongside experienced academic colleagues within Wrexham University. Experience across different Engineering programmes and teaching environments. Opportunities to contribute to Wrexham University’s international and TNE provision. Opportunities to develop international teaching experience and professional networks. Where international teaching is required, return international travel, accommodation, subsistence and appropriate local support in accordance with University arrangements. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Wrexham University is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion and welcomes applications from suitably qualified candidates from all backgrounds. We will make reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process where required. How to Apply To join our Engineering Sessional Lecturer Pool, please complete the application form and upload any supporting documents to outline your teaching and/or industry experience and engineering specialisms. Closing Date 7 th of September 2026 Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Engineering Location Wrexham Salary per hour Post Type Casual Closing Date Monday 07 September 2026 Reference 2526SESSPOOLENG Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2627006": {
      "title": "Digital Systems & AI Integration Associate (SMART Partnership Associate)",
      "description": "2627006 Digital Systems & AI Integration Associate (SMART Partnership Associate) - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2627006 Digital Systems & AI Integration Associate (SMART Partnership Associate) Digital Systems & AI Integration Associate (SMART Partnership Associate) Salary £33,000 plus £2,000 bespoke training budget Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract, to drive forward a project between Wrexham University and Flintshire County Council, based in St Davids Park, Ewloe, Flintshire We seek to employ a graduate in Computing, Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Science, Information Technology or related field who will lead the design, build, implementation and embedding of Flintshire County Council’s integrated AI decision support tool within frontline service delivery. Working with the Wrexham University’s Academic Supervisors and Flintshire County Council’s Digital Solutions Team, this role will transform how residents access help and support across the county. By co-developing an AI-powered information hub, the project will enable frontline staff within the Housing area to quickly and accurately match people with the services that best meet their needs, allowing caseworkers to support people directly and residents a smoother journey to the right support. In this role, you’ll apply AI and machine learning models, working with diverse data sets and using your organisational, teamworking, and communication skills to create a powerful and user-friendly tool which will ultimately provide valuable insights into service demand and gaps, supporting smarter commissioning and better use of public resources. Alongside Flintshire CC coaching and mentoring to develop your experience and understanding to complete the project successfully, there is a £2,000 bespoke training budget available to support the post-holder. Whilst there will be opportunity for the role holder to work flexibly they will work mainly from the Flintshire County Council offices in Ewloe and at Wrexham University on occasion. This appointment is made as a result of the approval of a Welsh Government-funded SMART Partnership with Flintshire County Council. Please note: Interviews will take place in person at Wrexham University For more information, please contact the Enterprise Office, email enterprise@wrexham.ac.uk Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Cyber and Computing Location Wrexham Salary £33,000\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Fixed Term 12 months Closing Date Monday 21 September 2026 Reference 2627006 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2627055": {
      "title": "Specialist Study Skills Tutor",
      "description": "2627055 Specialist Study Skills Tutor - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2627055 Specialist Study Skills Tutor Specialist Study Skills Tutor 22.5 hours per week, Term Time only (40 weeks per year) An exciting opportunity has arisen at Wrexham University to join our Inclusion Services and Disability Support Team as a Specialist Study Skills Tutor. In this role you will be expected to deliver high quality specialist, non-subject specific individually tailored study skills tuition to students who have Specific Learning Difficulties (SpLD), mental health conditions, autistic spectrum conditions, long term health conditions and physical and sensory impairments who are registered with the University Inclusion Services and Disability Support team. You will support students to develop a range of study skills strategies including organisational skills in order for them to manage their time and workload effectively. You will also support other strategies including memory, reading, note-taking, essay planning, exam revision skills and any other appropriate approaches. Our aim is to promote and implement an inclusive learning environment, enabling students to study independently and reach their potential. You will also contribute to the creation of resources and delivery of awareness training on good practice in supporting students who have Specific Learning Difficulties (SpLD) or other neurodivergent conditions to University academic and professional support staff. The successful candidate must be educated to Degree level or equivalent, with a recognised Dyslexia/SpLD related qualification and meet the specific qualifications/ and professional body membership requirements of the DfE Disabled Students Allowances (DSA) and Non-Medical Help (NMH) framework to deliver DSA specialist support. This includes Full Professional Membership of either PATOSS, BDA, ADSHE or Associate Dyslexia Guild Membership. If you would like to know more about the role, informal enquiries can be made by contacting Sarah Roberts (Head of Inclusion Services and Disability Support). Email: sarah.roberts@wrexham.ac.uk Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department Inclusion Location Wrexham Salary £16,266 to £18,756\n              per annum Post Type Part Time Term Time Hours per Week 22.5 Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Reference 2627055 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills 