    "https://jobs.wrexham.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=2627068": {
      "title": "People Team Assistant",
      "description": "2627068 People Team Assistant - Jobs at Wrexham Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use Study Student life International Business Connect Research About Home Login Register Cymraeg Toggle Menu Home Login Register Cymraeg Study Student life International Business Connect Research About This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Job Vacancies 2627068 People Team Assistant People Team Assistant We're looking for an organised and proactive People Team Assistant to join our friendly People Team. Supporting colleagues across the University, you'll provide high-quality HR administrative support throughout the employee lifecycle, from recruitment and onboarding to maintaining employee records and responding to queries. This is a varied and fast-paced role where you'll play an important part in delivering an efficient, professional and customer-focused service. About You You'll have previous administrative experience, excellent organisational skills and a keen eye for detail. Confident using Microsoft Office applications, you'll be able to manage multiple priorities, communicate effectively with a wide range of people and handle sensitive information with discretion. A positive, flexible approach and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential. Experience in HR, Higher Education or a relevant qualification would be advantageous. What We Offer In return, you'll join a supportive team environment where you'll have the opportunity to develop your HR knowledge and build a rewarding career. We are committed to staff wellbeing, professional development and creating an inclusive workplace where everyone can thrive. You will receive a starting annual leave entitlement of 37 days inclusive of Bank Holiday and fixed closure dates, an excellent contributory pension scheme, as well as many other staff benefits. Please ensure that all sections of the application form are completed as incomplete application forms will not be considered. If you would like to know more we would love to hear from you, please get in touch to Sara Edwards, Senior People Team Administrator by email sara.edwards@wrexham.ac.uk or Nathan Payne-Linforth, People Partnering Officer by email nathan.payne-linforth@wrexham.ac.uk . Further details Job Description - Welsh Job Description - English Email details to a friend Apply Online Wrexham University is an equal opportunities employer and positively encourages applications from suitably qualified and eligible candidates and will ensure applicants will not be discriminated against due to their protected characteristics under the Equality Act 2010. The University will make all efforts to meet your access requirements. Please contact our People Team as soon as possible to discuss any adjustments or assistance you may need to complete your application form, or to answer any queries you may have. We welcome applications in Welsh and English. Any applications submitted in Welsh will not be treated less favourably than applications submitted in English. Excellence, Inclusion, Collaboration, Transformation & Sustainability Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Programme/Department People Team Location Wrexham Salary £26,701\n              per annum Post Type Full Time Closing Date Sunday 06 September 2026 Reference 2627068 Welsh Language Skills Welsh language skills are desirable Apply Online Jobs at Wrexham Jobs Home Current Vacancies Guidance for Job Applicants About the University Campuses and Facilities Campus 2025 Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Staff Benefits Contact Us Job Notifications Jobs by Email Study with us Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Short courses Online Courses Apply Quick Links Contact Us Open days Virtual tours Online Shop Welcome Week Academic Timetable Staff & Students Student Portal Staff Portal Job Vacancies Contact Wrexham University, Mold Road, Wrexham, LL11 2AW 01978 290666 We welcome calls in Welsh or English. Rydym yn croesawu galwadau yn Gymraeg neu Saesneg. Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok © Wrexham University Accessibility Cookies Contact Us Terms of Use"
